3.1 Self-Attention Distribution Transfer

The attention mechanism [3] has been a highly successful neural network component for NLP tasks, which is also crucial for pre-trained LMs. Some works show that self-attention distributions of pre-trained LMs capture a rich hierarchy of linguistic information [19, 8]. Transferring self-attention distributions has been used in previous works for Transformer distillation [20, 38, 1]. We also utilize the self-attention distributions to help the training of the student. Speciﬁcally, we minimize the KL-divergence between the self-attention distributions of the teacher and student:

